fix(settings): picking an adb binary reports on the one you picked, not the one before it

`handleBrowse` committed the path and then immediately re-checked. The commit's applier fires
`void pushAdbConfigToBackend()` unawaited, and Tauri runs `set_adb_settings` and `recheck_adb_install` as independent
tasks, so the re-check could reach the backend first and answer about the OLD binary. That is exactly the stale status
the comment above it says the re-check exists to prevent.

The Browse pick now awaits the push before asking. Running the push twice costs a round-trip and changes nothing: it
re-reads both settings fresh and sends the same pair.

Cell: the two commands recorded in order, with the push deliberately resolving off the current tick so a broken
ordering can't pass by accident. `adb/DETAILS.md` gains the rule, since the next caller that changes a setting and then
asks about it has the same trap waiting.
